  "id": "entoptic",
  "term": "entoptic",
  "definition": "Entoptic refers to visual appearances that arise from processes within the eye itself rather than from objects in the outside world. The term is used for such internally produced sights, including effects caused by structures or activity in the eye casting patterns or sensations into vision.",
